Index: ProjectArchitecture

Purpose:
  Project-specific architecture state. Root .sdd/architecture/ defines
  reusable architecture knowledge (levels, patterns, scaling, availability,
  data, observability, networking, deployment). This file tracks the
  project's actual architecture decisions, components, data flow, and
  infrastructure.

  Architecture templates live at @../../../templates/_sdd/architecture/.

Owns: ./

ReadOrder:
   1  INDEX.sdd (this file — project architecture map)
   2  system.sdd (system architecture)
   3  components.sdd (component architecture)
   4  data.sdd (data architecture)
   5  infrastructure.sdd (infrastructure architecture)
   6  diagrams/ (architecture diagrams)
   7  ../../architecture/ (architecture knowledge base)

Rules:
  [PA1] Architecture decisions MUST be recorded in @../decisions/INDEX.sdd.
  [PA2] Architecture MUST match ProjectScale (bax ../../architecture/levels.sdd).
  [PA3] Architecture MUST satisfy SecurityLevel requirements (bax ../../security/levels.sdd).
  [PA4] Architecture MUST NOT violate overengineering/underengineering gates.
  [PA5] Component boundaries MUST align with domain boundaries.
  [PA6] Data flow MUST be explicitly documented.
  [PA7] Infrastructure MUST be specified for production deployments.
  [PA8] Architecture MUST be kept in sync with actual code (drift detection).

Components:
  System components and their relationships:

    Format:
      <component>:
        type: <BE|FE|MD|DB|INFRA>
        path: <code_path>
        responsibility: <description>
        depends_on: [<components>]
        api: [<endpoints>]
        data: [<data_stores>]

System:
  System-level architecture:

    Format:
      name: <system_name>
      description: <purpose>
      components: [<component_list>]
      data_flow: <description>
      external_dependencies: [<list>]
      deployment: <deployment_model>

Infrastructure:
  Infrastructure architecture:

    Format:
      provider: <VPS|AWS|Azure|GCP|On-prem|Hybrid>
      compute: <specification>
      network: <specification>
      database: <specification>
      cache: <specification>
      storage: <specification>
      monitoring: <specification>
      backup: <specification>

Diagrams:
  Architecture diagrams are stored here. Diagrams are generated FROM
  the architecture model, never hand-maintained as a second source
  of truth (bax ../../architecture/architecture.sdd -> DiagramAsOutput).

  Diagram types:
    #CTX   Context diagram
    #ARCH  Architecture diagram
    #FLOW  Data flow diagram
    #DEP   Dependency diagram
    #NET   Network diagram
    #DEPLOY Deployment diagram
    #CI    CI/CD diagram
    #OBS   Observability diagram
    #SEC   Security diagram

Navigation:
  Root: @../INDEX.sdd
  Project: @../PROJECT.sdd
  ArchitectureKnowledge: @../../architecture/INDEX.sdd
  Levels: @../../architecture/levels.sdd
  Patterns: @../../architecture/patterns.sdd
  Scaling: @../../architecture/scaling.sdd
  Data: @../../architecture/data.sdd
  Availability: @../../architecture/availability.sdd
  Observability: @../../architecture/observability.sdd
  Networking: @../../architecture/networking.sdd
  Deployment: @../../architecture/deployment.sdd
  System: @system.sdd
  Components: @components.sdd
  DataArchitecture: @data.sdd
  Infrastructure: @infrastructure.sdd
  Diagrams: @diagrams/
  Template: @../../../templates/_sdd/architecture/system.template.md
  Decisions: @../decisions/INDEX.sdd
  Tasks: @../tasks/INDEX.sdd
  Security: @../security/INDEX.sdd

State: +
  Note:
  This file is the project-specific architecture map. It points to
  detailed architecture files and references the root architecture
  knowledge base. Architecture decisions are recorded separately in
  @../decisions/INDEX.sdd.
